<title>RUSSIA: Russia banks' number to shrink soon - central bank.</title>
<headline>Russia banks' number to shrink soon - central bank.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of Russian banks will continue to fall and there will soon be less than 2,000 banks, First Deputy Chairman Alexander Khandruyev said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;In several months we shall see less than 2,000 banks,&quot; Khandruyev told a news conference. &quot;We suppose that in the next two to three years the downward trend in the number of banks will continue.&quot;</p>
<p>On February 1 there were 2,025 banks in Russia, compared to 2,263 last February, the central bank said in a recent bulletin. Analysts have long said that Russia is overbanked.</p>
<p>--Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
